  "lessons": [
    {
      "title": "Plan Ahead",
      "slug": "plan-ahead",
      "displayOrder": 10,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 288,
        "lessonOrder": 10
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\nThe key to success with this sweater is  planning.  The knitting is relatively easy, but the finished product will be greatly improved by planning the techniques you will use.\r\n\r\n<div class='embed-video-container'>\n<iframe src='https://player.vimeo.com/video/323922483' frameborder='0' webkitAllowFullScreen mozallowfullscreen allowFullScreen></iframe>\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 4624,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "exerciseAccordion",
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "<h3>Size Decisions - Perfect Fit</h3>",
                  "bodyHtml": "The pattern is offered in 2 size ranges - choose one and adjust for you!<br>\r\nWhen you build your custom pattern, you'll want to know the following. Don't worry, once you choose your size, you will be shown the standard dimensions.  You won't have to make any changes unless you choose to!<br>\r\n<hr>\r\n\r\n\r\nStart by printing a worksheet for your size (use it to make notes):<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<br><ol class=\"instruction-list\">\r\n<li><b>How long? (E)</b> Measure from center back to hem</li>\r\n<li><b>Upper Arm (G)</b> Check a sweater you love</li>\r\n<li><b>Sleeve Length (C)</b> Long, 3/4 or short sleeve - it's your choice!</li>\r\n<li><b>Finished Wrist (A)</b> We'll decide on cuff finish later</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/42/sideways_cardigan_PF.jpg\">\r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/42/arrow1.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "<h3>Design Decisions</h3>",
                  "bodyHtml": "<style>\r\nmark { \r\n  background-color: yellow;\r\n  color: black;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<b>Before you go any further ..... what yarn will you use?  What stitch pattern will you use?  These decisions may influence the following choices.</b><br>\r\n\r\n<ol class=\"instruction-list\">\r\n<li><mark>Side Slit:</mark> Consider adding slits on the sides of the cardigan for an updated look</li>\r\n<li><mark>Asymmetric Hem:</mark> Plan to add length to the back of the sweater at the side \"seams\"</li>\r\n<li><mark>Pockets:</mark> Pockets can add a practical finishing touch</li>\r\n<li><mark>Cuffs:</mark> What finishing technique do you want for the sleeves?</li>\r\n<li><mark>Curved hem:</mark> Add a designer touch</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/42/design_decisions.gif\">",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/42/arrow2.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "<h3>Techniques</h3>",
                  "bodyHtml": "We will cover techniques you need to know in the course. But for now, consider your previous choices and think through knitting this sweater.<br><ul>\r\n<li>Picture EVERY STEP</li>\r\n<li>Plan how you are going to do things BEFORE YOU START KNITTING!</li>\r\n<li>Be comfortable with new-to-you techniques BEFORE YOU START KNITTING!</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<ol class=\"instruction-list\">\r\n\r\n<li>Casting on: We recommend shaping the v-neck with short row increases and decreases. A tutorial on this technique will be included next week</li>\r\n<li>Front edge opening: How are you going to finish this? Crochet? I-Cord? Narrow Band? Wide Band? Knit on the machine? By Hand?  Decisions, decisions, decisions ... plan ahead!\r\n<li>Binding off: The armholes are shaped with Casting On and Binding Off. These need to be stretchy (but not sloppy).<br>If you only know 1 technique, plan to learn (and practice) some different methods that may be appropriate for your yarn and stitch pattern choices. these can be used for side slits if you choose</li>\r\n<li>Sleeve shaping: Do you want the decreases of the sleeve to be a design element? Consider Full-Fashioned Decreases.  Maybe you prefer to knit your sleeves from the top down (Some knitters feel that this is faster)</li>\r\n<li>Hem: How are you going to finish the hem of the sweater? Crochet? I-Cord? By hand? What about a sideways hem/facing? (A tutorial will be included)</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<hr>\r\n<b>At the very minimum, here are skills you MUST know:</b><br>\r\n<em>If you are unsure of your skills, practice BEFORE YOU START KNITTING</em><br>\r\n<ul class=\"lightlist\" style=\"list-style:none;\">\r\n<li>Knit, dress and accurately measure a swatch</li>\r\n<li>Casting on and binding off loosely</li>\r\n<li>Knitting in pattern (if you choose - a plain stockinette sweater can be beautiful!)</li>\r\n<li>Increasing (for the sleeves)</li>\r\n</ul>",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/42/arrow3.png"
                }
              ],
              "legacy": {
                "showText": null,
                "size": null
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 4625,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
