    {
      "title": "Your Success Depends on this",
      "slug": "your-success-depends-on-this",
      "displayOrder": 15,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 290,
        "lessonOrder": 15
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "we've spent a lot of time planning, practicing and thinking about knitting ... are you ready to do some \"real knitting\"?<br><strong>DON'T SKIP THIS SECTION!</strong> <br>Your success with this course AND your success with your knitting machine depends on your understanding and mastering the art of knitting gauge swatches.<br>Without a swatch we are knitting in the dark.\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>How is the final sweater going to feel in the yarn and stitch pattern you've chosen?</li>\r\n<li>Do you have enough yarn?</li>\r\n<li>Do you have enough needles on your machine for the size you chose?</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>SWATCHING IS NOT OPTIONAL</strong></p>\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://www.knititnow.com/images/blog_images/2017/swatching_is_not_optional.jpg\" /></div>\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 4634,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Swatching is NOT optional",
          "slug": "swatching-is-not-optional",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3346,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "293143036",
              "title": "SWATCH!",
              "legacySlot": 1,
              "legacyComponentId": 4662,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151858429",
              "title": "Knit a Gauge Swatch in less than 10 minutes",
              "legacySlot": 2,
              "legacyComponentId": 4662,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859471",
              "title": "Swatching in Pattern Knitting",
              "legacySlot": 3,
              "legacyComponentId": 4662,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Just  DO IT!",
          "slug": "just-do-it",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3354,
            "blockType": "VimeoMultiple"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\r\nMeasuring a swatch flat isn't always the best way to measure gauge.  Your knitting is going to be hanging on your body. Consider the weight of the entire piece of knitting. A 4\" square isn't representative of a 23\" long sweater.<br>This concept is <b>especially important</b> for our sideways knit cardigan.<br>I hung my tuck swatch, added a bit of weight and let it hang for a couple of days. By doing this, I can be confident in the stitch gauge and my sweater won't end up dragging on the floor when I wear it. <i class=\"fa fa-smile-o aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/42/tuck_swatch.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\t<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/42/please_watch.gif\">",
              "legacyComponentId": 4678,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "245117927",
              "title": "Gauge and Drop",
              "legacyComponentId": 4677,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Gauge and Drop",
          "slug": "gauge-and-drop",
          "order": 3,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3364,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\r\nI've used this diagonal tuck stitch for the body of my sweater and plain knitting for the sleeves.<br>\r\n\r\nThe pattern allows me to enter a different gauge for the body and the sleeves.<br>\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/42/multiple_gauge.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail zoom\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/42/plain_swatch.jpg\"><br>\r\n\r\n<hr>",
              "legacyComponentId": 4674,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "migrationPending",
              "legacyType": "StitchPattern",
              "notes": [
                "Unmapped legacy component type: StitchPattern"
              ],
              "legacyFields": {
                "CHALLENGE_ASSIGNID": "3355",
                "STITCHPATTERNID": "164",
                "STITCHPATTERN_IMAGE": "603",
                "TYPEOF": "StitchPattern"
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 4675,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Sue's Swatches",
          "slug": "sue-s-swatches",
          "order": 4,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3355,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Perfect Fit for YOU",
      "slug": "perfect-fit-for-you",
      "displayOrder": 17,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 292,
        "lessonOrder": 17
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Knit it Now Dynamic Patterns were created to give you the freedom to knit any pattern YOUR WAY!<br>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>ANY yarn!  Don't be limited to the yarn the designer chose</li>\r\n<li>Use ANY machine!</li>\r\n<li>ANY stitch pattern!  Easily substitute your favorite stitch pattern .. with NO MATH!</li>\r\n<li>Perfect Fit!   Adjust the dimensions of the pattern to fit YOU</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<br>\r\nUnlike software, Knit it Now Patterns are generated completely online.  Nothing to install, maintain, upgrade or learn!<br>\r\nEnter YOUR gauge, select your size and GET KNITTING!<br><ul>\r\n<li>Single size per printout (no more highlighting your size)</li>\r\n<li>Limited abbreviations ... written in plain terms!</li>\r\n<li>Custom sizing</li>\r\n<li>NO MATH</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 4663,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151858983",
              "title": "Using the Basic Blueprints",
              "legacyComponentId": 4664,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "{first} are you new to Knit it Now Dynamic Patterns?",
          "slug": "first-are-you-new-to-knit-it-now-dynamic-patterns",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3356,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "277783617",
              "title": "Armed with our dimensions, watch as we create our custom pattern",
              "legacyComponentId": 4665,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "How to Build a Pattern",
          "slug": "how-to-build-a-pattern",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3357,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n<div class=\"col-12-xs\"><br>\r\n<em>When I am packing cones of yarn in a box, I know the the size of the cones, but will the cones will fit in the available box?  To be able to mail your yarn order, <b>the BOX size is more important than the cone dimensions!</b><br>If the box is too big the cones will rattle around and the box will get crushed.  If the packaging is too small, the box could split in transit.<br><b>It doesn't matter what your bust, waist and hip measurements are ... what matters is the size of the package!</b></em><br></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-12-xs\"><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/42/nothing_fits/body_measure.jpg\"</div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-12-xs\">\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\"> <i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> INSTEAD OF MAKING A PATTERN FIT OUR DIMENSIONS, LETS DETERMINE A COMFORTABLE SIZE FOR OUR SWEATER AND KNIT THE SWEATER TO THOSE DIMENSIONS!</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-12-xs\">\r\nPrint and complete your Perfect Fit Template and record the dimensions of your favorite sweater.<br>Armed with your preferred garment measurements, you will create a knitting pattern to match your sweater.\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 4668,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "download",
              "label": "Print the Worksheet",
              "filename": "/downloads/worksheet3.pdf",
              "showInline": true,
              "legacy": {
                "assignId": "3358",
