        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\r\nWhen you get to the side seam, you may want to add a slit to your sweater.<br>Simply bind off 6-8\" at the hem edge and immediately cast on the same number of stitches again. Using a cast on rag helps make this easier.<br>Repeat on the other side seam for a designer touch.<br>\r\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o fa-2x aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> TIP: Make room for finishing by binding off, knitting a few rows, THEN cast back on.  This will create an opening so a crochet or I-cord edge will lay flat within the opening.\r\n\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/42/side_slit.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t",
              "legacyComponentId": 4680,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
