        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<h3>NOTE</h3>\r\nSince the original Knit-Along, we added a sideways sleeve to the pattern itself.  This worksheet is no longer needed ... (unless you LOVE to do your own  math) <i class=\"fa fa-smile-o aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <br>\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/42/sideway_sleeve.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\nBecause this is a sideways knit, stripes (or self-striping yarn) will be vertical in the body of the sweater.  Knit as written, the sleeves will have horizontal stripes.<br>Prefer the stripes to match the body?  You can easily chart the sleeves to be knit sideways as well.<br><ul>\r\n<li>Establish your sleeve dimensions</li>\r\n<li>Use the Knit it Now Slope tool for the shaping math</li>\r\n<li>Use Short Row Increases and Decreases to knit the sleeves</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 4719,
              "order": 1
            },
